{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/980612-looking-for-help-on-the-horror-of-changeling","id":980612,"title":"Looking for help on the horror of Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-02T23:54:35-07:00","id":980612,"title":"Looking for help on the horror of Changeling","content":"Can anyone recommend some movies or tv shows that can show the horror the changeling the lost. <br /> <br /> Can anyone also sell me on some of the horror of changeling the lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T00:02:32-07:00","id":980615,"title":"","content":"The Hallow is a fantastic horror movie that's based directly on legends about the fae and changelings. Pan's Labyrinth is another great pick. Hell, a lot of creepypastas are essentially modernized counterparts to the folkloric monsters that inspired Changeling. Persona 4 isn't a perfect fit, but it does have a serial killer murdering people by trapping them in a dangerous parallel labyrinth. Anything about alien abduction works too, since Changeling also encompasses ChroD's take on that. Dark Skies is a pretty good recent abduction movie. And of course there's a vast galaxy of Dark Fairytale Stuff out there to explore. If you're up to check out other tabletop games, JAGS Wonderland and Don't Rest Your Head are both FANTASTIC sources of changeling inspiration. <br /> <br /> And if you can't see the horror in changeling...I don't want to sound dismissive, but I can't really help you there. It's PTSD: The Game. It's about being kidnapped, having your soul and mind ripped into pieces and haphazardly glued back together, and finally fighting your way back to reality to find that no one even realized you were gone, there's a THING that looks like you living your life, and no matter how hard you try to return to the rational, normal world you were stolen from, you'll always have the shadow of the Hedge looming over you in one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-03-2016, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T00:27:02-07:00","id":980626,"title":"","content":"You were taken away and went through absolutely dehumanizing hell, and fought with everyhing you had to get away, only to get back... and discover nobody knows you were ever gone. There's a fake living your life, there's a monster patiently waiting to drag you back as soon as you make a mistake, and the person you see in the mirror is a scarred, broken thing that barely looks like your face anymore. When the world has moved on from you, when you can't trust your perceptions or sleep through the night anymore, when your only solace are other people as broken as you are... what do you do?<br /> <br /> Changeling's horror is masquerading as something alien and monstrous, but it's the experience that any abuse survivor or war veteran goes through every single day of their lives with a thin fae coat of paint on top. Either that'll resonate with you or you'll likely move onto something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T20:02:57-07:00","id":981228,"title":"","content":"Very first thing I would suggest is Pan's Labyrinth. Guillermo del Toro is a great fit for the fantasy-horror aesthetic of Changeling, and how the fantasy and the real world can be equally terrifying in totally different ways. Hellboy II is also good, it even has a goblin market.<br /> <br /> I dunno about anyone else, but when I was first getting into Changeling, the thing that stuck with me is &quot;fae stuff isn't real, but it's still dangerous.&quot; There's a really great illustration in one of the books of a Fairest in full-on David Bowie Goblin King mode, standing at the top of a staircase and pointing his enchanted rapier at a confused and terrified mailman trying to deliver coupons, and the chapter fiction is the Changeling speaking in vaguely Shakespearean tangled verse about how his rotting hoarder apartment is actually an opulent dream-castle, and put that phone down <i>don't you dare call 911 or I'll run you through, villain!</i><br /> <br /> You've been forced into a world of magical refugees playing at the Mad Tea Party, guys who used to have families and bills and favorite TV shows who now have glowing eyes and ram horns curling out of their foreheads and demand that you address them with the proper respect as <i>The Least Ignoble Knight of Spring</i>, and get viciously angry and challenges you to a duel at dawn when you tell them that's completely insane. These are your <i>allies. </i>This is the society you have to join and pretend to understand and learn the esoteric rules and secret oaths of if you don't want to be dragged back to Forever Nightmare Zone by a living story. It's the horror of being pushed off the deep end into a different world, and realizing that the only way to escape is <i>through</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:32:52-07:00","id":981461,"title":"","content":"Here's another part of the horror: <i>Anyone</i> could sell you out to the Gentry for their own protection. Probably the worst part is that on some level, you've thought about doing it. That's how you know everyone else has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:26:04-07:00","id":981606,"title":"","content":"One thing I think often gets lost in talking about the horror of Arcadia and the fear of going back, is there's a part of you - a horrible part of you that you can't stand and try to push down, but keeps coming back no matter how hard you try - actually <i>misses it</i>. And you tell yourself that's fucked up, and how could you ever even <i>think</i> that, and you beat yourself up over it.<br /> <br /> But try as you might, that feeling never goes completely away. The lingering thought that maybe if you went back, it would be better this time. Maybe your Keeper has changed. And even if they haven't, isn't it worth a little hurt to be able live in that wonderful, magical place again? As much as it hurt, wasn't that pain at least better than the nothing you feel in this place, where nothing has any magic to it and no one even knows or cares what you've been through?<br /> <br /> And then the guilt comes back, because what kind of fucked up do you have to be to actually want to ever feel that way again? Wake up, it was pure torture and nothing is worth living in that constant agony.<br /> <br /> And that's where <i>I'll never go back</i> gives way to <i>the long way home</i>. Somewhere between the pain you've been through and the emptiness you came back to, you can try to build a new place for yourself. Somewhere with just a touch of that magic that makes you wish you could go back, but with the safety and security of being the one in control of your own life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-04-2016, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:44:01-07:00","id":981621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/980612-looking-for-help-on-the-horror-of-changeling?p=981606#post981606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I think often gets lost in talking about the horror of Arcadia and the fear of going back, is there's a part of you - a horrible part of you that you can't stand and try to push down, but keeps coming back no matter how hard you try - actually <i>misses it</i>. And you tell yourself that's fucked up, and how could you ever even <i>think</i> that, and you beat yourself up over it.<br /> <br /> But try as you might, that feeling never goes completely away. The lingering thought that maybe if you went back, it would be better this time. Maybe your Keeper has changed. And even if they haven't, isn't it worth a little hurt to be able live in that wonderful, magical place again? As much as it hurt, wasn't that pain at least better than the nothing you feel in this place, where nothing has any magic to it and no one even knows or cares what you've been through?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, you had to <i>become a different person</i> to get out of Arcadia. The nature of the seeming curse is such that, in a very real sense, part of you is <i>still there</i>, because there is ultimately no other place it <i>could </i>go under its own power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:48:35-07:00","id":981625,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin has it right. I played a really fun one-shot once that ended with the party facing down a PC's former Keeper face to face, and to the shock of everyone else, the PC bounded right back to their side. The player hadn't telegraphed their character as a secret Loyalist or anything, but it made total sense and was a great horror beat at the climax.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T14:52:01-07:00","id":981706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/980612-looking-for-help-on-the-horror-of-changeling?p=981625#post981625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlaquin has it right. I played a really fun one-shot once that ended with the party facing down a PC's former Keeper face to face, and to the shock of everyone else, the PC bounded right back to their side. The player hadn't telegraphed their character as a secret Loyalist or anything, but it made total sense and was a great horror beat at the climax.</div> </div> </div> </div> Outstanding, perfectly done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T20:04:36-07:00","id":981921,"title":"","content":"How do I talk about the horror of Lost without making it a gigantic essay?<br /> <br /> Anything can change in an instant. Everything <i>will</i> change. Nothing is static, everything is falling, everything is falling apart. All you hold dear, all you stand for, is illusion and dream. Everything hurts and the only way to stop hurting is to retreat, to build your own wall of thorns and play tea with your shadows. Everything is a lie and the only solace you'll find is if you start believing them, others or your own.<br /> <br /> The world is too large and too fluid and too false for you to ever be enough or for you to have a place, &quot;for the world is more full of weeping than you can understand.&quot; You're lost, and you might never find home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T00:13:15-07:00","id":983802,"title":"","content":"Let's examine some of that PTSD angle. Specifically, what a Changeling has gone through.<br /> <br /> Nine times out of ten (which seems almost oxymoronic), the Keeper who abducted them seems completely inexplicable, and worse <i>unpredictable</i>. You've just been stolen from your life, taken to this inhuman being's home, and nothing makes sense. The rules you lived your whole life by no longer apply. You had to make contracts with fire to gain warmth and with food to gain nourishment, just to survive the first &quot;day&quot; (itself a nebulous concept in Arcadia).<br /> <br /> Moreover, every time you thought you had your new master figured out, they surprised you, and probably not in a pleasant way. How do avoid gaining their ire if you don't understand what could set them off? How do you please them when their desires and values seem to change from moment to moment? How do you keep from getting hurt, when they seem to find endless and unexpected ways and times to torment you?<br /> <br /> All patterns are false, all expectations ill-founded. No wonder sudden life changes can result in loss of Clarity. Every Changeling is not only suffering post-traumatic stress, but one based on the trauma of never knowing when, where, or how the pain will come. And it's no wonder Changelings wonder if they ever really escaped. It's not just a logical question, but an emotional response. If you were conditioned to never trust patterns - to live your fragile life always on edge - the comparatively safe and rational mortal world seems too good to be true. When will the other shoe drop?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 10-08-2016, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T06:49:14-07:00","id":983893,"title":"","content":"How about other then the PTSD angle where is the horror of the fea other then that ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T09:17:58-07:00","id":983945,"title":"","content":"Another good one IMHO would be the movie Ink, at least in some respects. I kind of think if you adapted it to a darker, more realistic approach the groundwork in Chronicles of Shannara could set up a world where the Fae once again hold sway. Other than the PTSD angle as far as I understand it, the horror is total loss of identity and societal context for said identity. It's like being Jason Bourne only worse. You weren't even just a weapon for someone else: that implies both having a purpose and/or having the ability to start anew in human society. As a Changeling, you were basically the toy of callous, manipulative Fae and now must hide from the world because on one side you have the Fae hunting you and on the other, in all likelihood a Fetch took your spot in your normal, everyday life and attempts to re-integrate into your family or even just some town or city will end in disaster once they realize what you are. Hence why Freeholds and the courts and such exist, because the Hedge looms on one side and humans who lash out at what they don't understand on the other. Does that make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T09:26:17-07:00","id":983946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/980612-looking-for-help-on-the-horror-of-changeling?p=983893#post983893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about other then the PTSD angle where is the horror of the fea other then that ?</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to choose between dreaming soundly in another dimension or not vanishing from sight whenever you fall asleep.<br /> <br /> You have to brave the dangers of that same other dimension on a fairly regular basis if you don't want a scrap of your soul falling into the wrong hands.<br /> <br /> You regain your hold on your perspective through maladaptive behaviors that the old you wouldn't have stooped to or by gambling with reminders of your trauma and hoping you can self-actualize your way through the resulting Holmesian hypersensitivity without being overwhelmed by sudden loud noises.<br /> <br /> Your principle means of mystical defense against being taken back to Faerie also makes you a much more attractive target and gives Fae and Huntsmen more cause to mess with your subordinate Courtiers and other changelings who didn't put as much of their new lives into being a dream-magical legend-character.<br /> <br /> Contrariwise, it is a truism that (Contracts and Hedge-travel to twist its flow notwithstanding) you have a finite amount of time to try and live a normal life, and the main benefit doing that offers also serves as another set of vulnerabilities to your capacity for parsing fae nonsense.<br /> <br /> To be fae is to live between a rock and a hard place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T10:43:28-07:00","id":983972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/980612-looking-for-help-on-the-horror-of-changeling?p=983946#post983946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have to choose between dreaming soundly in another dimension or not vanishing from sight whenever you fall asleep.<br /> <br /> You have to brave the dangers of that same other dimension on a fairly regular basis if you don't want a scrap of your soul falling into the wrong hands.<br /> <br /> You regain your hold on your perspective through maladaptive behaviors that the old you wouldn't have stooped to or by gambling with reminders of your trauma and hoping you can self-actualize your way through the resulting Holmesian hypersensitivity without being overwhelmed by sudden loud noises.<br /> <br /> Your principle means of mystical defense against being taken back to Faerie also makes you a much more attractive target and gives Fae and Huntsmen more cause to mess with your subordinate Courtiers and other changelings who didn't put as much of their new lives into being a dream-magical legend-character.<br /> <br /> Contrariwise, it is a truism that (Contracts and Hedge-travel to twist its flow notwithstanding) you have a finite amount of time to try and live a normal life, and the main benefit doing that offers also serves as another set of vulnerabilities to your capacity for parsing fae nonsense.<br /> <br /> To be fae is to live between a rock and a hard place.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Leliel's Horror Recognition Guide thread, Ziggy described the nature of the Wyrd as he sees it: It runs on conflict, and that includes internal conflict. You draw a moral line you won't cross. The Wyrd says &quot;Oh, really?&quot; and places a giant rock on the other side. &quot;How about now?&quot; It pushes the rock closer, &quot;How about now?&quot; Eventually, the other side of that line doesn't look so hard as the rock bearing down on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T10:44:42-07:00","id":983973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/980612-looking-for-help-on-the-horror-of-changeling?p=983972#post983972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Leliel's Horror Recognition Guide thread, Ziggy described the nature of the Wyrd as he sees it: It runs on conflict, and that includes internal conflict. You draw a moral line you won't cross. The Wyrd says &quot;Oh, really?&quot; and places a giant rock on the other side. &quot;How about now?&quot; It pushes the rock closer, &quot;How about now?&quot; Eventually, the other side of that line doesn't look so hard as the rock bearing down on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This guy gets it.<br /> <br /> There's always a world where you'll compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T12:00:38-07:00","id":983998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/980612-looking-for-help-on-the-horror-of-changeling?p=983946#post983946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have to choose between dreaming soundly in another dimension or not vanishing from sight whenever you fall asleep.<br /> <br /> You have to brave the dangers of that same other dimension on a fairly regular basis if you don't want a scrap of your soul falling into the wrong hands.<br /> <br /> You regain your hold on your perspective through maladaptive behaviors that the old you wouldn't have stooped to or by gambling with reminders of your trauma and hoping you can self-actualize your way through the resulting Holmesian hypersensitivity without being overwhelmed by sudden loud noises.<br /> <br /> Your principle means of mystical defense against being taken back to Faerie also makes you a much more attractive target and gives Fae and Huntsmen more cause to mess with your subordinate Courtiers and other changelings who didn't put as much of their new lives into being a dream-magical legend-character.<br /> <br /> Contrariwise, it is a truism that (Contracts and Hedge-travel to twist its flow notwithstanding) you have a finite amount of time to try and live a normal life, and the main benefit doing that offers also serves as another set of vulnerabilities to your capacity for parsing fae nonsense.<br /> <br /> To be fae is to live between a rock and a hard place.</div> </div> </div> </div>is that from 2ed? I dont remember none of that stuff in 1st. Specially the dreaming and dissapearing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/980612-looking-for-help-on-the-horror-of-changeling?p=983893#post983893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about other then the PTSD angle where is the horror of the fea other then that ?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my 2cents on the matter, i tend to reject this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/980612-looking-for-help-on-the-horror-of-changeling?p=983972#post983972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You draw a moral line you won't cross. The Wyrd says &quot;Oh, really?&quot; and places a giant rock on the other side. &quot;How about now?&quot; It pushes the rock closer, &quot;How about now?&quot; Eventually, the other side of that line doesn't look so hard as the rock bearing down on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because i never liked the Wyrd as this sort of force that is out there to mess with your character or as an narrative-trope-inducing-force of nature. So to me the horror, and keep in mind i dont like to enforce it neither, is what you are now. As an example movie i would say look to Cruel intentions, the crappy movie with Sarah Michelle Gellar.<br /> <br /> Like the protagonist of that movie you need to provoke a reaction. You might see people as people but you also see them as button you gotta push to get what you need glamour. You are now the kind of people that incite violence just for violence sake. Or play with people emotions (love, lust, despair) seemingly just because. Not doing so means living a life as much as prisioner as before following weird catches just to have power to defends yourself. So you will seduce a girl and break her heart just to get that sweet despair or watch gleefully as to men beat each other to death while getting off from the anger in the air.<br /> <br /> I always picture the more wyrd you get the more you look at people like this<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/S/cmx-images-prod/Image/33244/AUG090089-06._QL80_TTD_.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I couldnt find a better image than this, but i mean the one upper center pannel. But again im fairly entrenched on 1st edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 10-08-2016, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T12:09:00-07:00","id":984000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/980612-looking-for-help-on-the-horror-of-changeling?p=983998#post983998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is that from 2ed? I dont remember none of that stuff in 1st. Specially the dreaming and dissapearing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That part is specifically a 2e thing, yes. Since dreams are physical places for Changelings, they have to choose when the sleep between dreaming (and in so doing physically enter the space that is their dream) or not dreaming (and in so doing not have restful sleep). The rest of Satchel's post is not exclusively 2e, as the things he mentions were true of 1e as well, but 2e does emphasize them much more in its mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T17:42:36-07:00","id":984135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/980612-looking-for-help-on-the-horror-of-changeling?p=983893#post983893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about other then the PTSD angle where is the horror of the fea other then that ?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ExWfh6sGyso\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ExWfh6sGyso\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ExWfh6sGyso\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ExWfh6sGyso </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T17:41:41-07:00","id":989629,"title":"","content":"I recommend you check out Baroness Nerak's AP here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...se-actual-play</a><br /> <br /> Even just reading through the backstories for the PCs should give you a good sense of the horror.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, watch Return to Oz. It's a very dark sequel to Wizard of Oz that is pretty perfect for showing some Changeling horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T10:09:37-07:00","id":990472,"title":"","content":"For themes of being replaced/altered, loss of sense of reality, abduction, and paranoia: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_Skies_(film)\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Skies</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honeymoon_(2014_film)\" target=\"_blank\">Honeymoon</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boogeyman_(film)\" target=\"_blank\">Boogyman</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/They_(2002_film)\" target=\"_blank\">They</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Identity_(film)\" target=\"_blank\">Identity</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goodnight_Mommy\" target=\"_blank\">Goodnight Mommy</a><br /> <br /> Also check this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TV Tropes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings are no longer entirely human, having been tormented in positively <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Creator/HPLovecraft\" target=\"_blank\">Lovecraftian</a> ways until they were broken in either body, mind, soul, or all of the above, and then rebuilt according to the True Fae's whims.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 10-20-2016, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:14:13-07:00","id":990537,"title":"","content":"Here's another horror tidbit- using your Kewl Powerz is inherently dangerous and destabilizing. You can control the elements, you can turn into a bird, you can hulk out into an extra-magical form- but every time you do so, you're pushing yourself further away from reality. You decide you won't use your powers at all? Too bad, they're the only thing standing between you and the Gentry. Besides, you can't turn off being a Changeling. You'll always see the antlers in the mirror, you'll always feel the Wyrd at work- even if you're improbably lucky enough that no one comes after you.<br /> <br /> And if you really want to make things dark? Have your players start as Fetches. You know stories where people are confronted with twisted, monstrous reflections of themselves? That's the life of a Fetch- except in your personal Persona 4, the Shadow really is your true self. That twisted monster that embodies everything you've ever feared about yourself? It's the real you, and you're a cheap copy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-30-2016, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T16:36:04-07:00","id":990682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/980612-looking-for-help-on-the-horror-of-changeling?p=990472#post990472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For themes of being replaced/altered, loss of sense of reality, abduction, and paranoia: <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_Skies_(film)&amp;quot;]Dark</a> Skies[/URL], <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honeymoon_(2014_film)&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Honeymoon</a>, <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boogeyman_(film)&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Boogyman</a>, <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/They_(2002_film)&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">They</a>, <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Identity_(film)&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Identity</a>, <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goodnight_Mommy&amp;quot;]Goodnight</a> Mommy[/URL]<br /> <br /> Also check this<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah I love that qoute, I've been saying for awhile that Changeling is very Lovecraftian tonewise, not the &quot;pantheon&quot;, I mean you could make Cthulu a True Fae, but more in the sense of themes like body horror, alien horrors that twist and break the mind, ect...,but all that horror is clothed in fairy tales, folk tales, and such in order to interact with reality. <br /> <br /> Imagine Snow White with the soul of Hastur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}